TAM-HIDE - WORKSTATION PRIVACY FOR TAMLINUX

tam-hide locks a Tamlinux workstation cleanly and without disclosing account
or session details.

Version 0.2.0 implements Phase 1/1b (`tam-hide` Wayland `ext-session-lock-v1`
locker for `tam-pane` with PAM fallback and idle output blanking/wake via
`ext_idle_notifier_v1` and `zwlr_output_power_manager_v1`) and Phase 2a
whole-seat authentication and lock-confirmation plumbing:

- Privileged Argon2id (`libargon2`, default m=65536 KiB, t=2, p=1) salted
  slow-hash passcode store (`passcode_store`, `tam-hidectl passcode-*`) with
  constant-sweep matching across all accounts.
- `tam-hided` session registry and compositor lock-confirmation gate (refuses
  VT handoff away from an active graphical session until `CONFIRM_LOCK` fires),
  plus a privilege-separated `auth.sock` with active-session `SO_PEERCRED`
  gating, server-side exponential lockout, and single-use 128-bit `PICK` tokens.
- `tam-hide` `--ready-fd`, `--auth-socket`, `--session-vt`, and post-auth
  multi-account/session picker UI (`LOCK_UI_PICKER`).

Phase 2b (disposable KVM/QEMU VM end-to-end verification with real
`VT_LOCKSWITCH` and multi-VT handoff) is required before installing
`tam-hided.service` on a live workstation.

Follows the tam-idol 1.3.0 standard.

WHERE THINGS ARE

  src/        Wayland locker (tam-hide), VT seat controller (tam-hided), CLI (tam-hidectl)
  tests/      unit tests and headless tam-pane integration test
  sandbox/    nested tam-pane demo for manual verification
  arch/       security and compositor design
  plans/      implementation phases
  work/       current handoff and session records
  ROADMAP.md  planned milestones
  UPSTREAM.md upstream code and references
